Diagonal-action follow-up (2026-09-09)
------------------------------------
Baseline: 9acae35, including the lifetime changes measured above.
Current: row/column scaling in layer_modes_2d and sp_modes_2d, with
cosine/sine vectors reused by the 2D ETM and SMM paths. These replace
eight dense N-square products in the left blocks and sixteen in rotation.
The grazing guard's eight repeated left-block products also become scaling.
The ETM block identity still has quadratic per-layer allocation cost.
No eigensolve, inverse, Fourier order, cutoff threshold or declaration changed.
No dependency was installed, updated or copied.

Paired timing and allocation reproduction:
Load the fixed degree-8 affine FEM projection at cap=64, quadrature_refine=40,
as described above, checking its profile with load_projection. For each
retained order (8,8) and (12,12), call projected_matrices once. Build the
public solver's order_kxy arrays for lattice=700*[[1,.45],[0,.7]], wavelength=900,
theta=.2, phi=0, top=1, bot=2.25. Give those same arrays and convolution
matrices to the parent and current solve_2d functions, loaded under separate
module names in the same process. Pass n_top=1, n_bot=1.5, incidence=(0,1).
Use either one 300 nm layer or three identical 100 nm layers, repeating
each convolution slot along its layer axis. This splits the same physical
stack while exercising multiple layer solves.

Warm each function once per configuration with answers=amplitude. Run
six pairs at order 8 and four at order 12, alternating which function
runs first. Collect garbage before each call. Time only solve_2d, with
perf_counter, without tracemalloc. Summaries compare every p/s R/T order
from all calls with the saved baseline warm-up arrays, and check R+T=1.
After the timing pairs, trace separate amplitude and field calls with fresh
tracemalloc traces following garbage collection; capture live/peak bytes
before accessing the output, then stop the trace and discard the result.
Inputs and imports precede each trace; native LAPACK workspace is excluded.
No other numerical work from this task overlaps the measurements. Unrelated
host load is uncontrolled; NumPy/SciPy use Apple Accelerate, with the same
OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 and OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 settings and their limitations.

